      "title": "Faculty, Computer Science & AI - Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Job Opportunities | Rivier University Career Opportunities For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Faculty, Computer Science & AI - Program Coordinator | Rivier University Career Opportunities page has loaded. Faculty, Computer Science & AI - Program Coordinator | Rivier University Career Opportunities page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Job Opportunities Menu Job Opportunities Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Rivier University Career Opportunities powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Faculty, Computer Science & AI - Program Coordinator Print Apply ﻿ Faculty, Computer Science & AI - Program Coordinator Location Nashua Job Type Full-Time Job Number 202500183 Division Division of Arts and Sciences Department Computer Science Opening Date 02/01/2026 Description Benefits Description Coordinator, Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence Program Rivier University invites applications for the position of Coordinator of the Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence (CS/AI) Program . The Coordinator will provide academic leadership, program oversight, and industry-informed guidance for Rivier’s undergraduate and graduate programs in Computer Science and Artificial Intelligence. This role blends teaching, curriculum development, student mentoring, and the creation of substantial external partnership building to ensure that Rivier’s CS/AI programs remain innovative and aligned with evolving industry needs. The ideal candidate brings broad industry experience, a strong professional network, and a demonstrated commitment to excellence in technology education. Duties and Responsibilities Program Leadership and Coordination · Oversee the planning, development, delivery, and continuous improvement of Computer Science and AI programs. · Lead curriculum review and advancement to ensure academic quality and industry alignment. · Coordinate course scheduling, adjunct faculty assignments, and program assessment activities. · Maintain compliance with institutional policies and accreditation standards. Teaching and Student Engagement · Teach courses in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, or related fields at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. · Advise and mentor students academically and professionally. · Support recruitment, retention, and student success initiatives. Industry and Community Partnerships · Cultivate and sustain relationships with employers, research partners, and industry leaders. · Facilitate internship pathways, experiential learning, and applied project opportunities. · Bring real-world insights and industry trends into program design and classroom instruction. Strategic Advancement · Collaborate with faculty and university leadership to expand the visibility and impact of CS/AI programs. · Support initiatives related to grants, innovation labs, workforce development, or emerging technologies. · Represent Rivier University at professional conferences, events, and regional partnerships. Qualifications · Doctorate degree in a relevant field, or a master’s degree in a relevant field with commensurate industry experience reflecting advanced expertise. · A robust professional network in technology, AI, or related domains. · Experience with curriculum development and program coordination. · Background in applied AI, machine learning, cloud computing, cybersecurity, or software architecture. · Evidence of effective teaching · Strong communication and collaboration skills. Supplemental Information Applicants should apply online and include a cover letter along with resume/CV at: https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/rivieredu/jobs/5220625/faculty-computer-science-ai-program-coordinator All applications and nominations will be considered highly confidential. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Rivier University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, age, veteran or marital status, sex sexual orientation, gender identity, or disability in admission or access to, treatment in, or employment in its programs and activities, and Title IX requires that the University not discriminate on the bases stated above. In addition to a competitive salary, Rivier University offers full-time employees a comprehensive benefits package which includes medical, dental and vision coverage, employer paid life and disability plans, retirement plan with employer match, Health Reimbursement Arrangement (HRA), Health Savings Account (HSA) with employer contribution, flexible spending accounts, paid time off, holidays, educational assistance benefits, employee assistance program (EAP) and a variety of additional discounts and services. To learn more details, vist our Summary of Benefits . Employer Rivier University (NH) Address 420 South Main Street Nashua, New Hampshire, 03060 Phone 603-897-8717 603-897-8211 Website https://www.rivier.edu/ Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Job Opportunities Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under t